{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Designer Loop.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Designer Loop.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"designer loop designer loop","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Designer Loop.md","fileName":"Designer Loop.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Designer Loop","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Design Methods]] [[Iterative Game Design Cycle]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","Iterative Game Design Cycle","Balancing Loop","Game-Player System","Prototype","Playtesting","advancedgamedesign.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Designer Loop.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Designer Loop.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"designer loop designer loop","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Designer Loop.md","fileName":"Designer Loop.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Designer Loop","heading":"Designer Loop","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The designer loop is the cycle in which a designer changes a game, observes players interacting with it, compares their experience with the design intent, and revises the design. It acts as a [[Balancing Loop]] around the [[Game-Player System]].\n\nThe loop cannot close through rules or a simulation alone; it requires actual player interaction. [[Prototype|Prototypes]] and [[Playtesting]] supply the evidence by which the designer reduces the gap between intent and experience.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","Iterative Game Design Cycle","Balancing Loop","Game-Player System","Prototype","Playtesting","advancedgamedesign.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Designer Loop.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Designer